    "root_cause_explanation": "In Historical B vs A, Seed 3 (|diff|=0.0263) and Seed 73 (|diff|=0.0263) tie for absolute rank. Standard fractional tie ranking assigns rank 13.5 to both. Under the true conditional permutation test conditioned on the observed ranks (including the tie at 13.5), there are exactly 276,128 combinations out of 2^30 with rank sum <= 71.5. The mathematically exact two-sided permutation p-value is p = 5.143285e-4 (0.000514). SciPy's method='exact' reported 0.000555 because it evaluates W=72 against the theoretical distribution assuming integer ranks without ties (P(W <= 72 | no ties) = 297,870 / 2^30 = 0.000555). Both results demonstrate significant degradation (p < 0.001); the conditional permutation test p = 0.000514 is the mathematically exact value under the observed data."
  },
